  "slug": "automated-microscopy-2e31",
  "summary": "New OT-based segmentation and deconvolution tools (Tracel, spOT-NMF) plus SWIMR and ARCADE target how spatial counts map to cells, types and states.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is attributing spatial transcriptomic measurements to cells and cell types. Tracel reassigns transcripts or bin counts to cells via two-stage optimal transport against matched scRNA-seq references, unifying segmentation across platforms. spOT-NMF applies OT-regularized NMF for reference-free deconvolution with proximity-aware niche mapping. SWIMR integrates multiple reference panels with spatial correlation, and ARCADE separates cell-type abundance from continuous intratype transcriptional state. SpatioCAD's cell-density-aware graph diffusion reduces false-positive spatially variable genes in heterogeneous tissue. A second thread concerns dynamics. SPECHTacle combines Waddington-OT with Shannon entropy to flag preferentially altered populations, and BioTrajX scores pseudotime plausibility through directionality, order-consistency and endpoint metrics. In glioblastoma, GlioTrace tracks single-cell invasion state transitions ex vivo, while scDORI infers enhancer-driven GRNs from multiome data. Imaging benchmarks and tools (DynaCell, Organotchi) and VLM-guided scATAC gene activity scoring (VIGAT) are adjacent.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-08"
}
